{"from": "claim:lk-08-10-isaiah-6-quoted", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-13-14-15-isaiah-6-quoted", "note": "Both Evangelists apply Isaiah 6:9-10 to the parables audience; Matthew quotes a fuller form of the text."}
{"from": "claim:lk-08-10-isaiah-6-quoted", "type": "related_to", "to": "text:isaiah-6-9-10", "note": "Isaiah 6:9-10 is the passage quoted (biblical cross-reference, not evidence)."}
{"from": "claim:lk-08-38-39-proclaimed-in-city", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mk-05-20-proclaimed-decapolis", "note": "Mark sends the man through the Decapolis; Luke keeps him in his own city."}
{"from": "claim:lk-08-42-only-daughter-twelve", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mk-05-42-girl-twelve", "note": "Luke gives the age at the request (about twelve) and calls her an only child; Mark gives it at the healing."}
{"from": "claim:lk-08-42-only-daughter-twelve", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-09-18-ruler-office", "note": "Matthew's ruler's daughter has just died; Luke's is dying when Jairus asks."}
{"from": "claim:lk-08-51-inside-with-parents", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mk-05-37-peter-james-john-inside", "note": "Luke admits the father and mother besides Peter, John and James; Mark names only the three."}
{"from": "claim:lk-08-52-53-mourners", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-09-23-flute-players", "note": "Matthew adds flute players and disorder; Luke has only the weeping and mourning crowd."}
{"from": "claim:lk-08-03-joanna-wife-of-chuza", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-28-01-mary-from-magdala", "note": "Luke 8:3 names Joanna among the women; Matthew 28 has no Joanna at the tomb."}
{"from": "claim:lk-08-26-country-of-gadarenes", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-08-28-country-of-gergesenes", "note": "Luke reads Gadarenes (WEB) with Gerasenes in P75/B/D; Matthew reads Gergesenes (WEB) - the manuscripts of all three Synoptics vary among the same three names."}
{"from": "claim:lk-08-26-country-of-gadarenes", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mk-05-01-gadarenes-region", "note": "Luke (WEB: Gadarenes) and Mark (WEB: Gadarenes) share the name; Mark's oldest manuscripts read Gerasenes."}
{"from": "artifact:joanna-ossuary", "type": "documented_by", "to": "source:wikipedia-joanna-chuza"}
{"from": "artifact:joanna-ossuary", "type": "documented_by", "to": "source:wikipedia-biblical-figures-identified"}
{"from": "artifact:joanna-ossuary", "type": "documented_by", "to": "source:wikipedia-biblical-figures-identified-dispute"}
{"from": "artifact:joanna-ossuary", "type": "attests", "to": "person:joanna", "grade": "D", "note": "The ossuary inscribes a first-century Jerusalem woman 'Johanna (Yehohanah), granddaughter of Theophilus the High Priest' (published by Barag and Flusser, Israel Exploration Journal 36, 1986); the identification with Luke's Joanna is expressly uncertain - Johanna was the fifth most popular woman's name in Judaea."}
{"from": "artifact:joanna-ossuary", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:lk-08-03-joanna-wife-of-chuza", "grade": "D", "note": "Same disputed identification: the ossuary names another Joanna (granddaughter of Theophilus, high priest 37-41 CE), and the name's popularity blocks an identification; it attests the name, not the wife of Chuza."}
{"from": "text:josephus-ant-17-13-steward", "type": "documented_by", "to": "source:wikisource-ant17-steward"}
{"from": "text:josephus-ant-17-13-steward", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:lk-08-03-herods-steward", "grade": "C", "note": "Josephus shows the office inside the Herodian house: Caesar 'called for Archelaus's steward, who took care of his affairs at Rome' - a steward (epitropos) managing a Herodian ruler's affairs in the same generation; it does not name Chuza."}
